{"slug": "tricolor-salad-alla-splendido", "nyt_id": 1016140, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1016140-tricolor-salad-alla-splendido", "name": "Tricolor Salad Alla Splendido", "author": "Jeff Gordinier", "description": "An Italian restaurant standard is kicked up a few notches in this recipe from Mario Carbone, the chef at Carbone restaurant in New York. If you find it hard to track down Italian frisée or various types of radicchio, you can substitute the usual trio of arugula, endive and radicchio. A helping of poached tuna adds richness and a hint of a salade niçiose. Jeff Gordinier", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 40, "raw": {"total": "PT40M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "8 ounces raw tuna steak", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "raw tuna steak", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "Salt and freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt and freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 lemon", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "lemon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 bay leaves", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "bay leaves", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "2 cups plus ½ cup extra-virgin olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "plus ½ cup extra-virgin olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "8 ounces various types of radicchio, like Castelfranco, Tardivo, Treviso or Rosa di Gorizia", "group": null, "quantity": 8.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "various types of radicchio", "preparation": "like Castelfranco, Tardivo, Treviso or Rosa di Gorizia", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "4 ounces frisée, Italian if possible", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "oz", "item": "frisée", "preparation": "Italian if possible", "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "¼ cup large capers (packed in salt, rinsed and soaked a half-hour)", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "large capers (packed in salt", "preparation": "rinsed and soaked a half-hour)", "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "⅓ cup small pitted olives, preferably taggiasca", "group": null, "quantity": 0.3333333333333333, "unit": "cup", "item": "small pitted olives", "preparation": "preferably taggiasca", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "½ cup golden raisins, rehydrated in 1 cup boiling water", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "golden raisins", "preparation": "rehydrated in 1 cup boiling water", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "2 tablespoons lime juice", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "lime juice", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "¼ cup chopped parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "chopped parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "1 bunch chives, minced", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "bunch", "item": "chives", "preparation": "minced", "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Cut tuna into 4 even portions; season both sides with salt and pepper. With a peeler, cut 4 long strips from skin of lemon; place in a small pot with the bay leaves and tuna. Add about 2 cups oil, or enough to just cover the tuna. Over medium heat, bring oil to about 140 degrees and gently poach for 10 minutes, adjusting or turning off heat to maintain temperature, until tuna is cooked through. Turn off heat and allow tuna to cool in the oil for 10 minutes. Cut into ¼-inch slices."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Wash and dry all greens well. Keep leaves whole and place in a large bowl."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Heat remaining ½ cup oil in a small saucepan with the capers, olives and raisins. Once they begin to fry lightly and become aromatic, add tuna slices and pour mixture over the greens. Juice the lemon and add 2 tablespoons juice, along with lime juice, parsley and chives. Toss well and season with salt and pepper to taste. Divide among 4 plates and serve immediately."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 1355.25, "protein_g": 16.7, "carbohydrates_g": 23.3, "fat_g": 136.7, "saturated_fat_g": 19.1, "unsaturated_fat_g": 14.5, "trans_fat_g": null, "cholesterol_mg": 22.1, "sodium_mg": 815.8, "fiber_g": 3.9, "sugar_g": 13.2, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["italian"], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-lunch-main-course-salad-side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["olive", "radicchio", "tuna"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/03/19/dining/20140319-TORRISI-slide-LJU9/20140319-TORRISI-slide-LJU9-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "Tricolor salad alla splendido.", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/03/19/dining/20140319-TORRISI-slide-LJU9/20140319-TORRISI-slide-LJU9-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "Tricolor salad alla splendido.", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 44}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2014-03-19", "scraped_at": "2026-09-07T00:05:41Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "triggerfish-with-pistou-and-garden-vegetables", "nyt_id": 1013021, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/1013021-triggerfish-with-pistou-and-garden-vegetables", "name": "Triggerfish With Pistou and Garden Vegetables", "author": "Christine Muhlke", "description": "Christine Muhlke", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 70, "raw": {"total": "PT1H10M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 cups water", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "cup", "item": "water", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 large carrot, peeled and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "large carrot", "preparation": "peeled and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "½ medium onion, peeled and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": null, "item": "medium onion", "preparation": "peeled and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "1 small shallot, peeled and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "small shallot", "preparation": "peeled and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "1 leek, cleaned and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "leek", "preparation": "cleaned and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 6, "raw": "¼ medium fennel bulb, whole with fronds", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": null, "item": "medium fennel bulb", "preparation": "whole with fronds", "optional": false}, {"position": 7, "raw": "1 fresh bay leaf", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": null, "item": "fresh bay leaf", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 8, "raw": "½ bunch fresh parsley", "group": null, "quantity": 0.5, "unit": "bunch", "item": "fresh parsley", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 9, "raw": "2 teaspoons sugar, plus more to taste", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "tsp", "item": "sugar", "preparation": "plus more to taste", "optional": false}, {"position": 10, "raw": "2 small garlic cloves, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "small garlic cloves", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 11, "raw": "¼ cup white wine", "group": null, "quantity": 0.25, "unit": "cup", "item": "white wine", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 12, "raw": "Various seasonal market vegetables", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "various seasonal market vegetables", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 13, "raw": "2 bunches basil, leaves removed", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": "bunch", "item": "basil", "preparation": "leaves removed", "optional": false}, {"position": 14, "raw": "1 clove garlic, peeled and chopped", "group": null, "quantity": 1.0, "unit": "clove", "item": "garlic", "preparation": "peeled and chopped", "optional": false}, {"position": 15, "raw": "Salt", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 16, "raw": "freshly ground pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "freshly ground pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 17, "raw": "4 tablespoons olive oil", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": "tbsp", "item": "olive oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 18, "raw": "4 triggerfish fillets (see note)", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "triggerfish fillets", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 19, "raw": "Cayenne pepper", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "cayenne pepper", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 20, "raw": "Canola oil", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "canola oil", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 21, "raw": "Juice of 1 lemon", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "juice of 1 lemon", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 22, "raw": "Various seasonal herbs", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "various seasonal herbs", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 23, "raw": "greens", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "greens", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 24, "raw": "edible flowers (flowers optional)", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "edible flowers", "preparation": null, "optional": true}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Combine the first 11 ingredients in a large pot. Simmer for 25 minutes. If using right away, strain and move on to Step 2. Otherwise, the broth can be cooled and stored, unstrained, in the refrigerator for up to 1 week."}, {"position": 2, "text": "Preheat the oven to 300 degrees. Wash the vegetables and peel, if necessary. They can be prepared in any or all of the following ways: cooked in the broth until tender and left whole; cooked in the broth until tender and then puréed with broth; or left raw and shaved with a mandoline or peeler. Utilizing all three of these methods makes for a beautiful presentation."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Bring a medium pot of salted water to a boil. Have a bowl of ice water ready. Blanch the basil for 2 seconds. Quickly remove and immerse in the ice water. Strain and put in a blender with the garlic clove, salt, pepper and sugar to taste; add plenty of broth to keep the purée spinning. When it’s smooth, slowly drizzle in 2 tablespoons of the olive oil to emulsify. Strain, reserving the bright green broth. Discard the solids."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Season the fish fillets with salt and cayenne. Heat a large sauté pan over high heat. Add enough canola oil to cover the bottom. When the oil shimmers, add 2 fillets to the pan, skin side up, and do not disturb. Cook until golden brown, 3 to 5 minutes. Place on a baking sheet, skin side down. Repeat with the remaining 2 fillets. When all the fillets are seared on one side, drizzle with 2 tablespoons olive oil and a little lemon juice. Place the baking sheet in the oven and cook until the fish is opaque throughout, 6 to 8 minutes."}, {"position": 5, "text": "Ladle the pistou into 4 warm bowls. Divide the vegetables among them, reserving some of the shaved ones. Place the warm fish on top of the vegetables. Garnish with herbs, greens, edible flowers (if desired) and remaining shaved vegetables."}], "nutrition": null, "tags": {"cuisine": [], "diet": [], "course": ["dinner-main-course"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["spring"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/03/dining/Triggerfish/Triggerfish-superJumbo.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://static01.nyt.com/images/2014/04/03/dining/Triggerfish/Triggerfish-facebookJumbo-v2.jpg", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": null, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "2010-01-31", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:34:25Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
{"slug": "troisgros-potatoes-gratin", "nyt_id": 10017, "url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/recipes/10017-troisgros-potatoes-gratin", "name": "Troisgros Potatoes Gratin", "author": "Bryan Miller, Pierre Franey", "description": "", "servings": {"text": "4 servings", "min": 4, "max": 4, "yield_type": "servings"}, "time": {"prep_minutes": null, "cook_minutes": null, "total_minutes": 30, "raw": {"total": "PT30M"}}, "ingredients": [{"position": 1, "raw": "4 medium-size Idaho or Washington potatoes, peeled and halved", "group": null, "quantity": 4.0, "unit": null, "item": "medium-size idaho or washington potatoes", "preparation": "peeled and halved", "optional": false}, {"position": 2, "raw": "1 ½ cups whole milk", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "whole milk", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 3, "raw": "1 ½ cups heavy cream", "group": null, "quantity": 1.5, "unit": "cup", "item": "heavy cream", "preparation": null, "optional": false}, {"position": 4, "raw": "2 garlic cloves, peeled", "group": null, "quantity": 2.0, "unit": null, "item": "garlic cloves", "preparation": "peeled", "optional": false}, {"position": 5, "raw": "Salt to taste", "group": null, "quantity": null, "unit": null, "item": "salt to taste", "preparation": null, "optional": false}], "steps": [{"position": 1, "text": "Slice each potato section into disks about a quarter-inch thick. Slice each disk in half widthwise. Do not wash."}, {"position": 2, "text": "In a saucepan over medium-high heat, combine milk, cream, garlic and salt. Bring to a boil, add potatoes, reduce heat to medium and cook for about 10 to 15 minutes or until they are semifirm but not too soft. Remove with a slotted spoon and set aside."}, {"position": 3, "text": "Over medium heat, reduce milk mixture to about a cup. Discard garlic."}, {"position": 4, "text": "Arrange potatoes in individual gratin dishes. Evenly distribute milk mixture over them. Before serving, place under a broiler until potatoes are golden brown."}], "nutrition": {"source": "nyt", "basis": "per_serving", "calories": 525.5, "protein_g": 9.9, "carbohydrates_g": 44.7, "fat_g": 35.4, "saturated_fat_g": 22.3, "unsaturated_fat_g": 1.7, "trans_fat_g": 1.1, "cholesterol_mg": 110.0, "sodium_mg": 919.1, "fiber_g": 4.5, "sugar_g": 9.0, "computed_with": null}, "tags": {"cuisine": ["french"], "diet": [], "course": ["casseroles-side-dish"], "meal": [], "occasion": [], "other": ["easy", "fall", "five-ingredient", "heavy-cream", "milk", "quick", "russet-potato"]}, "images": [{"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x675.png", "alt": "", "primary": true}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x900.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}, {"url": "https://cooking.nytimes.com/assets/recipe-wallpaper/wallpaper-1200x1200.png", "alt": "", "primary": false}], "rating": {"average": 4.0, "count": 12}, "video_url": null, "comment_count": null, "published_at": "1995-07-12", "scraped_at": "2026-09-06T22:25:04Z", "scraper_version": "1.0.0"}
